			"notes": "Field Emitters 1.2.0 adds datapack presets, KubeJS integration and eleven translations, with fixes for network settings, redstone control and cross-loader behavior.\n\n### New features\n\n- Datapack field presets and reusable filters, operator commands, and persistent preset locks.\n- Optional server-side KubeJS controls and events on NeoForge 1.21.1 and Forge/Fabric 1.20.1. Forge/Fabric 1.21.1 support datapacks without KubeJS integration.\n- Spanish, French, German, Japanese, Simplified Chinese, Traditional Chinese, Brazilian Portuguese, Russian, Korean, Polish and Italian translations.\n- Relative inside/outside direction rules for enclosed perimeters.\n\n### Fixes and improvements\n\n- Keep settings consistent through linking, reconnection and world loads, including disabled fields.\n- Preserve unrelated changes when multiple managers edit a field.\n- Let one redstone input control a connected field while retaining saved input-face rules.\n- Trigger detection output immediately and refresh active pulses instead of queueing them. Crossing counts remain independent.\n- Preserve management access on restart and improve network identity handling during relocation.\n- Enforce link distance, stop matching phasing mobs, and correct Fabric energy consumption and Forge packaging.\n- Improve tuner layout, status messages, tooltips and translated text fitting.\n\n### Downloads\n\nChoose the jar matching your Minecraft version and loader:\n\n- Minecraft 1.20.1: Forge or Fabric\n- Minecraft 1.21.1: NeoForge, Forge or Fabric\n\nZeroMods Core 0.1.1 is bundled. **You do not need a separate Core download.** Client and server should use matching Field Emitters versions. Existing loader/API dependencies still apply.\n\nThe release includes SHA-256 checksums and a source-commit manifest for all five builds."
		},
